  "SNAPSHOT of the cloud voice catalog, read-only from staging on 2026-10-15. This is the",
  "generator's input: which real provider voice each personality speaks in.",
  "",
  "🔴 WHY A SNAPSHOT AND NOT A LIVE QUERY. The generator runs on a laptop with database",
  "credentials; the thing it produces is committed into a PUBLIC repo. Pinning the input",
  "means the audio files and the mapping that produced them land in the same commit, so",
  "anyone can see which voice a sample claims to be without database access. A live query",
  "would make the output unreproducible and the provenance unreadable.",
  "",
  "⚠️ IT GOES STALE SILENTLY. Nothing here notices when the catalog changes. Refresh with",
  "the query in scripts/gen-voice-samples.mjs's header and re-run the generator; the",
  "manifest records the date so a sample's age is always legible.",
  "",
  "MEASURED, and the reason John's ruling needed its second half: the cast is SPLIT across",
  "two providers. 7 personalities are ElevenLabs, 3 are Inworld (butler/pirate/princess),",
  "so an ElevenLabs key alone unlocks neither Butler nor Pirate nor Princess until each has",
  "an ElevenLabs alternate (tts_voices.alt_provider, migration 202610151900, VH).",
  "",
  "'dashie' is voice_mode=preferred, not fixed - the household's own TTS choice outranks it.",
  "Its sample therefore demonstrates ONE voice (RACHEL) and must be labelled as the default",
  "Dashie voice, never as 'what Standard sounds like'."
 ],
